# Research content

Hidden `/research` library (phase 1). Email capture inbox (phase 2). Not in nav or footer. `noindex` + sitemap exclude via `isStagedPath` until an explicit go-live.

## Capture vs library

| Layer | Where | Who writes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Inbox** | R2 `art-adamsimms-xyz-research` (`inbox/…`) | Worker `art-adamsimms-xyz-research` via `research@adamsimms.xyz` |
| **Library** | `src/content/research/*.md` | You (or phase 3 admin promote) |

Capture is freeform (link, PDF attach, or linked file URL). The Worker stores evidence and enqueues **deep enrichment** (OG, reader excerpt, bib, Wayback, Workers AI suggestions, graph hints). It **never** creates markdown nodes. See [docs/RESEARCH-INBOX.md](../../docs/RESEARCH-INBOX.md).

Binaries never live in git — attachments stay on research R2 (`attachments` frontmatter URLs after promote).

## Enrichment

- Queue: `art-adamsimms-xyz-research-enrich` (inbox Worker produces + consumes; admin re-enrich produces)
- Suggestions + provenance live on inbox `meta.enrichment`; promote is human-confirmed
- Prefer existing `tags` / `collections` from `library/index.json`; LLM may propose `newTags` separately
- Graph hints also use `site/works.json` + `site/writing.json` (rebuild via admin or after promote)
- Reader/PDF excerpts are triage aids — do not dump full HTML/PDF text into git

## Slug stability

- `slug` is a **permanent ID** once anything links to it (`relatedResearch`, future map)
- Prefer a better `title` over renaming `slug`
- If a rename is required, update every inbound `relatedResearch` (and any hard-coded links) in the same change

## One node per URL

- At most one **non-private** node per normalized `url`
- To add a source to another set, use `collections` and/or `relatedResearch` — do not duplicate the file
- Build fails on duplicate public URLs (`assertUniqueResearchUrls` in `src/lib/research.ts`)

## Collections vs tags

- `tags` — associative / topical
- `collections` — intentional sets (membership); one file, many collections

## Types

`book` · `essay` · `artwork` · `person` · `concept` · `place` · `archive` · `film` · `other`

There is no `link` type — use the `url` field on any type.

## Status

`note` → `developed` → `core`

## Private

`private: true` omits the node from the index, `getStaticPaths`, and sitemap. No auth-walled preview in phase 1.

## Attachments

`attachments` point at hosted files on research R2. Binaries never live in git.

## Related graph

- `relatedResearch` — other research slugs (backlinks computed at build as “Linked from”)
- `relatedWorks` / `relatedWriting` — site slugs (`/` and `/writing/`)

## Phase 3a (admin)

Access-gated UI at `/research/admin` (Worker `art-adamsimms-xyz-research-admin`): triage inbox, promote → git commit on default branch, edit/delete library files. Not linked from public nav.
